{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And the Egyptians will hear, for You have brought up by Your power, etc., and they will say to the inhabitants of this land.</b> After he mentioned ושמעו ואמרו (\"and they will hear\" and \"they will say\"), he explained the hearing and said: ״שמעו כי אתה ה' בקרב העם הזה אשר עין בעין נראה אתה ה'״ — they will hear that You, YHWH, are in the midst of this people, that eye to eye You, YHWH, are seen — in the manner of what is written (Exodus 24:17): ״ומראה כבוד ה' כאש אוכלת״." "<b>And the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote</b> by way of truth: עין (\"eye\") is an expression of appearance, as in (Numbers 11:7) ״ועינו כעין הבדולח״, (Ezekiel 1:27) ״וארא כעין חשמל״ — that is to say, He whose appearance is seen in appearance, that is Your great Name; and so you find in Ezekiel (43): ״וכמראה המראה אשר ראיתי בבאו לשחת העיר״ — end of quote." "<b>And what</b> Moses answered here — ״ושמעו מצרים״ — and likewise in the matter of the calf (Exodus 32:12): ״למה יאמרו מצרים״ — it would appear from this that were it not for the claim of the Egyptians, Moses would have borne the annulment of Israel for his own benefit, that he would become a great nation; and he certainly should have answered that he does not want his own benefit at the cost of Israel's annulment, for he had already surrendered his soul on their behalf, as he said (Exodus 32:32): ״מחני נא מספרך״. But Moses' intention in this prayer was to say: the Egyptians will calculate and say that there is power in the gods of Canaan to deliver from Your hand, for You executed judgments upon Egypt and upon their gods until You brought the people out from its midst, but You were unable to do so against the gods of Canaan — and so there will be a profanation of the Name, and the hands of transgressors will be strengthened, and the Egyptians will say to the men of the land of Canaan: מבלתי יכלת ה' — \"because YHWH was unable,\" that is, there is power and ability apart from the power of Israel. And because of the profanation of the Name Moses was unwilling to accept his own benefit of becoming a great nation through Israel's annulment. And this is what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: תשש כחו כנקבה — \"his strength weakened like a female's\" — for the female is acted upon and receives power from the male, since they would say that the power of Israel is not the Cause of causes, for behold there is another power that overcomes it and acts upon it like the power of the male that acts upon the female. So explained the great Rabbi, our Rabbi Shimon."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "Ezekiel citation written as (מ״ג) resolved to Ezekiel 43; the quoted phrase is Ezekiel 43:3."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:16.606549365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}